      "description": "<p>Israel Journal of Mathematics is an active peer-reviewed academic journal covering all areas of mathematics. It was established in 1951 and is published 6 times a year by Springer.</p>\n\n<p>This journal focuses on pure and applied mathematics and showcases research contributions from leading mathematicians worldwide, serving as a platform for disseminating mathematical research and fostering collaborations within the global mathematical community.</p>\n\n<p>The journal publishes original research articles, survey papers, and in-depth expositions that cover various areas of mathematics encompassing diverse branches, including algebra, geometry, analysis, number theory, combinatorics, mathematical logic, applied mathematics, and interdisciplinary topics. It features rigorous mathematical proofs, innovative methodologies, and novel mathematical insights that contribute to advancing mathematical knowledge.</p>\n\n<p>The ISSN is: 0021-2172</p>",
